      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Elevated LDL-cholesterol levels mean increased risk for coronary heart disease. In different studies the indication for decreasing high LDL-cholesterol in patients with coronary heart disease was proven. This is also the case with patients suffering from high LDL-cholesterol but not yet coronary heart disease. It is supposed that with longer duration of studies the total mortality between verum and placebo groups will also reach significance."},
